WEBVTT

00:03.002 --> 00:08.008
DEPARTMENT OF DIETETICS INTERVIEW VENUE

00:08.091 --> 00:09.467
Please have a seat.

00:10.010 --> 00:10.844
Thank you.

00:11.928 --> 00:16.057
Mr. Hase, I see that you have been
working at a restaurant for three years.

00:16.933 --> 00:21.688
What have you learned, or how did you grow
as a person during your time there?

00:26.401 --> 00:28.486
Working in the restaurant business

00:29.070 --> 00:31.573
has made me realize how much joy

00:32.699 --> 00:35.201
comes from feeding people,
and how much of an impact

00:35.952 --> 00:38.288
food has on the mind and body.

00:39.039 --> 00:41.291
Out of all the onigiri I've had in Japan,

00:41.374 --> 00:42.667
this is the best.

00:42.751 --> 00:43.793
It's good.

00:44.711 --> 00:46.838
Your cooking is the best!

00:46.921 --> 00:48.214
It was so delicious!

00:48.298 --> 00:51.176
It has a very deep flavor.

00:52.260 --> 00:53.428
From now on,

00:55.055 --> 00:58.433
I want to use all of my experiences
to my advantage,

00:59.809 --> 01:02.020
whether I fail or succeed,

01:02.896 --> 01:05.940
and support all athletes in any situation

01:06.024 --> 01:07.734
through the meals that I make.

01:10.779 --> 01:13.239
That's the kind of person
I wish to become.

01:14.115 --> 01:18.286
TANOMI

01:20.830 --> 01:22.415
-Hello.
-Hello.

01:23.917 --> 01:25.126
How was your interview?

01:27.003 --> 01:30.423
I was able
to say everything that I prepared.

01:31.007 --> 01:31.841
That's good.

01:37.430 --> 01:38.973
This place lets you enroll

01:39.057 --> 01:42.602
in a special class for sports dietetics
from your second year.

01:43.269 --> 01:46.773
And their scholarship program
is a lot more generous than I expected.

01:47.398 --> 01:48.566
There's even an overseas training program.

01:48.650 --> 01:49.818
Really?

01:49.901 --> 01:51.861
Wow…

01:55.782 --> 02:00.411
CLOSED

02:00.495 --> 02:04.791
TANOMI

02:06.376 --> 02:11.673
OPEN

03:24.621 --> 03:27.290
You're still sleeping?

03:27.373 --> 03:28.291
Here.

03:28.374 --> 03:30.043
I bought you breakfast.

03:31.502 --> 03:34.047
Just ten more minutes…

03:34.589 --> 03:38.968
Hey, aren't you going
to your intern job today?

03:49.562 --> 03:52.565
So it all depends on your presentation
for the contest, huh?

03:52.649 --> 03:53.483
Yeah.

03:55.193 --> 03:58.154
Wow, you're amazing, Rin.

03:58.238 --> 04:00.114
You're doing
your graduation project too, right?

04:00.823 --> 04:02.200
But I'm having fun.

04:03.159 --> 04:06.663
I've always thought that
creating art was something you do alone.

04:06.746 --> 04:09.207
But at work, everyone shares their ideas

04:09.290 --> 04:12.877
and shares the work
and operates as a team. So it's really…

04:16.673 --> 04:18.174
What's the word again?

04:19.467 --> 04:22.220
Oh, right! I feel a sense of fulfillment.

04:40.488 --> 04:42.156
ORGANIC INGREDIENTS
DERIVED FROM DANDELIONS

05:11.269 --> 05:12.103
So cute!

05:12.186 --> 05:14.147
-It's getting better and better.
-Yeah.

05:14.230 --> 05:16.607
-It's so cute.
-I really like it.

05:16.691 --> 05:18.151
The necktie is great!

05:18.234 --> 05:19.277
Yeah.

05:20.778 --> 05:22.739
It just needs a little something more…

05:23.448 --> 05:25.033
For example…

05:25.116 --> 05:26.284
Ms. Park,

05:26.367 --> 05:29.078
how about adding an accent color here?

05:29.162 --> 05:30.663
Maybe something like silver?

05:31.664 --> 05:32.623
I see.

05:33.249 --> 05:35.418
Thank you. I'll try that.

05:36.294 --> 05:37.670
It will make it even better.

05:57.106 --> 05:58.524
A DANDELION FAIRY THAT SOLVES SKIN ISSUES

05:58.608 --> 06:00.943
"Kindness, gently blooming on your skin."

06:01.027 --> 06:04.030
We took your catchphrase
and combined it with…

06:07.033 --> 06:09.077
‎A CHICK THAT WAS BORN FROM A DANDELION
‎POPOPIYO

06:11.204 --> 06:15.958
the color and shape of a dandelion,
which is a main ingredient,

06:16.042 --> 06:17.502
to come up with Popopiyo.

06:19.462 --> 06:22.965
Popopiyo is a chick
that was born from a dandelion.

06:23.049 --> 06:27.220
Despite his cute appearance,
he is actually mischievous

06:27.303 --> 06:31.557
and bold and loves to travel
around the world.

06:32.558 --> 06:37.313
And he also helps people
with their skin issues.

06:37.396 --> 06:38.231
‎MERCHANDISING EXAMPLES

06:38.314 --> 06:42.777
Popopiyo is
a likeable and heartwarming character.

06:42.860 --> 06:45.029
I am certain that it will appeal

06:45.113 --> 06:47.490
to the people in Japan
in their teens and twenties,

06:47.573 --> 06:49.826
which is our target demographic.

06:52.870 --> 06:55.665
That is all for my presentation.

06:55.748 --> 06:56.916
‎THANK YOU VERY MUCH!

06:56.999 --> 06:58.835
Thank you very much.

06:58.918 --> 07:00.711
Okay, thank you.

07:09.887 --> 07:11.431
That's an interesting idea.

07:11.514 --> 07:14.684
Thank you for working on that
in such a short time.

07:21.315 --> 07:22.692
Gamsahamnida.

07:31.200 --> 07:33.453
Thank you very much.

07:33.536 --> 07:35.455
All right, well then…

07:35.538 --> 07:36.747
That's awesome!

07:37.457 --> 07:39.542
It's so cute!

07:39.625 --> 07:41.377
I'm sure you'll get a good response!

07:41.461 --> 07:42.712
Thank you.

07:43.546 --> 07:44.589
Wow…

07:45.965 --> 07:47.592
That reminds me…

07:47.675 --> 07:50.052
Your enrollment results
come in soon, right?

07:50.136 --> 07:51.387
Yeah.

07:51.471 --> 07:55.266
But the number of openings
for working adults is limited,

07:55.349 --> 07:58.311
so to be honest, I might not get accepted.

08:00.062 --> 08:01.647
I'm pretty worried about that.

08:04.317 --> 08:07.361
And plus, as I was studying,
I realized that

08:07.987 --> 08:12.200
there is so much more to learn about food
than I had imagined.

08:13.910 --> 08:17.413
It feels like I'm starting my training
all over again.

08:19.624 --> 08:23.419
It seems like both of us
are always in training.

08:24.003 --> 08:25.254
That's true.

08:26.422 --> 08:29.509
But I feel like I can gain

08:30.009 --> 08:33.888
a different perspective,
once I get past this.

08:33.971 --> 08:38.142
I understand that feeling.
It's exciting to have a wall to climb.

08:38.226 --> 08:39.852
It means we can level up.

08:40.937 --> 08:43.439
I have to work hard
on my graduation project

08:43.523 --> 08:44.941
and job hunt too.

08:47.652 --> 08:48.486
Hey, Rin…

08:52.365 --> 08:54.825
I know you're looking
for a job in Japan but…

08:57.495 --> 08:59.080
Does your mother know about this?

09:05.378 --> 09:08.798
What happened to that instructor position?

09:11.467 --> 09:15.972
I do have to respond to her
about that soon but…

09:16.597 --> 09:17.890
I kind of…

09:19.141 --> 09:21.018
don't have the courage.

09:23.271 --> 09:27.608
Is that because she might be against it?

09:40.788 --> 09:43.916
Since this is the path you chose
after so much contemplation,

09:44.709 --> 09:46.711
if you are honest and tell her,

09:47.670 --> 09:51.048
I'm sure your mother will understand.

09:52.842 --> 09:54.010
It will be all right.

10:03.227 --> 10:06.939
Once I get the results for the contest,
I'll contact eomma.

10:20.077 --> 10:22.371
Here, it's the ekiben you've been
dreaming about.

10:22.455 --> 10:23.831
Really?

10:23.914 --> 10:25.625
-You bought it for me?
-Yeah.

10:26.459 --> 10:28.586
You said you saw it in an anime, right?

10:28.669 --> 10:31.088
Yeah, it's always been my dream.

10:32.298 --> 10:33.716
Thank you, Taiga.

10:44.018 --> 10:46.479
Wow! It's a real ekiben!

10:50.608 --> 10:51.442
Here.

10:58.616 --> 10:59.659
How is it?

11:00.409 --> 11:01.744
It's good.

11:04.246 --> 11:06.457
Ekiben is good even when it's cold.

11:07.833 --> 11:09.126
Taiga, eat with me.

11:09.752 --> 11:12.004
Okay, I'll try it too.

11:19.178 --> 11:20.971
-I'm full.
-Baebulleo.

11:27.478 --> 11:31.273
We were able to check one more thing
off your bucket list.

11:32.942 --> 11:34.151
That's right!

11:45.496 --> 11:48.749
Wait, you've done
more than half of them already.

11:50.251 --> 11:51.544
Thanks to you.

12:04.181 --> 12:05.141
‎Hey.

12:07.560 --> 12:08.644
It's too bad.

12:10.062 --> 12:12.940
Your proposal made it pretty far, though.

12:17.570 --> 12:18.446
Ms. Park?

12:20.197 --> 12:21.407
I'm sorry.

12:22.950 --> 12:24.493
Thank you.

12:26.579 --> 12:30.583
It was a nice experience for me
and I learned a lot.

12:35.629 --> 12:36.922
You know,

12:37.006 --> 12:41.093
it was so much fun and so exciting.

12:41.177 --> 12:44.555
I feel like this is the kind of job
that I want to do.

12:49.643 --> 12:51.812
I'm sure you will, Ms. Park.

12:53.022 --> 12:53.856
What?

12:53.939 --> 12:56.025
I can see a sparkle in your eyes.

12:59.403 --> 13:02.364
Whatever you are feeling right now,
don't forget it.

13:04.116 --> 13:05.034
Yes.

13:05.826 --> 13:07.453
Thank you.

13:08.704 --> 13:11.624
Thank you for everything
you've done for me.

13:11.707 --> 13:14.585
No, thank you.

13:15.419 --> 13:17.922
I'll do my best to find a job.

13:19.840 --> 13:21.967
Isn't it too late
to start job hunting now?

13:23.052 --> 13:24.970
You graduate in two months.

13:25.054 --> 13:27.431
Is anybody hiring new grads still?

13:28.015 --> 13:29.308
Yeah…

13:29.391 --> 13:32.520
The window for hiring new grads
is basically closed,

13:33.145 --> 13:38.359
so I will be mainly
looking for mid-career recruitments.

13:41.320 --> 13:43.405
What if none of the companies
want to hire you?

13:45.074 --> 13:47.910
Even if that happens,
I'll just do everything that I can.

13:48.827 --> 13:51.205
I won't lose focus anymore.

13:52.831 --> 13:56.001
For now, I'm making a list
of advertising companies in Japan

13:56.085 --> 13:59.421
and analyzing
their different business styles.

13:59.505 --> 14:00.965
You're serious, aren't you?

14:02.174 --> 14:04.093
You have a different look about you.

14:09.265 --> 14:10.391
All right then.

14:11.016 --> 14:14.186
After all, it's the first time you've
decided to do something on your own.

14:15.938 --> 14:19.984
Up until now, it seemed like you were
just doing things out of obligation.

14:21.944 --> 14:23.696
Yung-yeol…

14:24.905 --> 14:26.448
Do what you feel is right.

14:26.991 --> 14:28.409
I'll be rooting for you.

14:30.077 --> 14:31.036
Okay.

14:33.330 --> 14:37.251
MAMAMON

14:43.799 --> 14:45.718
Now is the time to do it.

14:57.980 --> 15:01.692
Oh, why are you calling at this hour?

15:01.775 --> 15:03.777
Have you eaten already?

15:04.486 --> 15:05.863
Yeah, I just ate.

15:07.698 --> 15:10.951
About the instructor position
you talked about…

15:11.911 --> 15:14.246
You finally made up your mind?

15:14.330 --> 15:15.706
You're taking it, right?

15:17.625 --> 15:18.751
I'm sorry,

15:19.293 --> 15:22.296
but I want you to turn it down.

15:23.547 --> 15:24.423
What?

15:25.090 --> 15:27.927
I want to work in advertising.

15:28.010 --> 15:29.929
So I'm going to look for a job in Japan.

15:33.015 --> 15:34.224
Wait a second.

15:34.308 --> 15:37.811
Looking for a job in Japan?

15:38.395 --> 15:40.564
And in advertising?

15:40.648 --> 15:43.651
What happened to animation?

15:43.734 --> 15:46.153
It may seem like I made a detour,

15:46.654 --> 15:50.699
but it's because I majored in animation
that I found an interest in advertising.

15:51.367 --> 15:52.368
Anyway,

15:53.202 --> 15:55.746
I'm going to do my best to find a job.

15:58.165 --> 15:59.291
Hello?

16:22.731 --> 16:25.192
Huh? Are you moving or what?

16:27.569 --> 16:29.113
Not right away.

16:29.780 --> 16:31.156
But soon.

16:31.240 --> 16:32.449
Really?

16:32.533 --> 16:34.535
Then this time,

16:34.618 --> 16:37.329
I'd like a place that's closer
to the station.

16:41.333 --> 16:44.420
It's not going to be around here.

16:45.462 --> 16:50.676
Oh, really? A new town? How exciting.

17:06.483 --> 17:08.277
It's open! Just come in!

17:12.114 --> 17:15.200
Tada! It's a good luck treat!

17:15.868 --> 17:18.120
Mochi? You made it, Rin?

17:18.787 --> 17:19.621
‎Yeah.

17:20.456 --> 17:22.207
It's called chapssal-tteok.

17:23.000 --> 17:26.837
Usually, you're supposed to gift it
to someone before their entrance exam.

17:26.920 --> 17:28.297
I'm sorry it's late.

17:28.380 --> 17:30.007
Don't be.

17:30.090 --> 17:32.634
Thank you for making it for me.

17:34.470 --> 17:36.597
It's because you looked so worried.

17:37.890 --> 17:40.893
You know how mochi
is really sticky, right?

17:40.976 --> 17:43.896
So you give it to them in hopes that

17:43.979 --> 17:47.149
success sticks to them like mochi.

17:47.232 --> 17:48.859
I see.

17:49.443 --> 17:51.278
Do you put red bean paste inside
or something?

17:51.361 --> 17:54.990
Yeah. Cocoa powder, red bean paste,

17:55.074 --> 17:58.285
and wal… walnuts go inside.

17:58.368 --> 18:00.996
I know it's going to be kkulmat already.

18:01.580 --> 18:02.956
There you go again with "kkulmat."

18:03.874 --> 18:05.334
Oh? Hold on…

18:07.294 --> 18:08.670
Stop playing around.

18:08.754 --> 18:11.173
-Sorry, sorry.
-Stop it.

18:14.718 --> 18:16.261
It might be documents from my work.

18:17.179 --> 18:18.972
I can accept the delivery.

18:19.056 --> 18:20.682
Will you do that? Thank you.

18:20.766 --> 18:21.934
Okay.

18:23.644 --> 18:25.354
Yes, yes, coming!

18:29.066 --> 18:31.068
Who are you?

18:33.237 --> 18:35.989
This is my daughter's room.

18:38.367 --> 18:39.368
Mom!

18:53.757 --> 18:56.718
Mom, this is my boyfriend.

19:00.514 --> 19:01.723
Annyeonghaseyo.

19:03.851 --> 19:05.018
Nice to meet you.

19:05.686 --> 19:06.687
Um…

19:07.354 --> 19:09.940
Jeoneun Hase Taiga imnida.

19:13.819 --> 19:15.154
"Boyfriend"?

19:16.238 --> 19:19.950
Here I thought you were
working hard on your graduation project,

19:20.033 --> 19:21.535
not bringing a man home!

19:21.618 --> 19:23.579
Don't say it like that.

19:23.662 --> 19:24.538
Park Rin,

19:24.621 --> 19:28.417
why do you think I let you study abroad?

19:28.500 --> 19:31.461
Why do you think I have been

19:31.545 --> 19:34.631
supporting you this whole time?

19:34.715 --> 19:37.968
I paid for your rent and living expenses
for what?

19:38.927 --> 19:42.097
It's so that you can focus on studying.
Isn't that right?

19:42.181 --> 19:44.808
It's not like I'm slacking off at school.

19:45.559 --> 19:49.354
Taiga and I are supporting each other,
and he helps me.

19:50.480 --> 19:52.608
Oh, is that right?

19:52.691 --> 19:55.819
Then why have you been hiding it from me?

19:55.903 --> 19:58.197
Because I knew you'd be like this!

19:59.948 --> 20:01.658
You don't have to overreact like that.

20:04.995 --> 20:08.040
Sorry, Taiga. Can you leave for today?

20:08.123 --> 20:09.249
What?

20:09.875 --> 20:11.627
I'll talk to her.

20:13.879 --> 20:15.214
Okay.

20:15.964 --> 20:17.341
I'll contact you later.

20:36.318 --> 20:37.945
You're going to find a job in Japan?

20:38.028 --> 20:40.280
What are you even thinking?

20:40.364 --> 20:42.532
Like I said, I want to try it out.

20:43.659 --> 20:45.452
And advertising at that?

20:45.535 --> 20:48.580
What was the point of studying
animation this whole time?

20:48.664 --> 20:52.542
You're only saying that
to be with your boyfriend, aren't you?

20:52.626 --> 20:57.965
Why would you make a decision
on a whim like that?

20:58.048 --> 21:00.884
It's not on a whim!

21:00.968 --> 21:03.220
I thought hard about it
and chose this path.

21:03.303 --> 21:04.972
How many times must I tell you?

21:05.055 --> 21:07.266
Life isn't that easy!

21:08.392 --> 21:10.644
Going into the advertising industry now?

21:10.727 --> 21:12.187
There's no way you'll succeed.

21:16.275 --> 21:17.317
Whatever.

21:17.818 --> 21:20.654
I don't have time to be
playing along with your whims.

21:20.737 --> 21:23.782
Once you graduate,
you will return to Korea right away.

21:28.912 --> 21:30.831
Mom, I've had enough.

21:31.873 --> 21:33.083
Excuse me?

21:34.126 --> 21:36.461
You've been suffocating me like that
this whole time.

21:36.545 --> 21:38.505
When you don't even know anything.

21:38.588 --> 21:42.926
I'm not a child anymore.
I can't stand you meddling in my life.

21:43.010 --> 21:45.304
It's my life, so just leave me alone!

22:21.089 --> 22:22.090
Hello?

22:22.174 --> 22:25.886
Taiga, what should I do?
Eomma still isn't back.

22:25.969 --> 22:26.928
What?

22:27.679 --> 22:29.931
It's because I said
horrible things to her.

22:48.658 --> 22:49.826
Ma'am!

22:51.078 --> 22:52.370
Oh, I'm sorry.

23:05.092 --> 23:06.843
Oh, excuse me!

23:07.427 --> 23:08.970
Have you seen this person?

23:10.305 --> 23:11.932
Okay, thank you.

23:43.505 --> 23:44.673
Ma'am!

23:45.507 --> 23:46.633
Um…

23:46.716 --> 23:47.592
Ma'am…

23:47.676 --> 23:48.969
um…

23:49.636 --> 23:52.139
Rin! Rin is waiting for you.

23:55.934 --> 23:57.686
What are you here for?

23:59.688 --> 24:00.689
Yes?

24:06.403 --> 24:08.280
It's just as they say.

24:08.363 --> 24:10.282
Children don't know
how their parents feel.

24:12.951 --> 24:16.371
She talks about finding a job
like it's so simple.

24:16.913 --> 24:20.250
But what if she can't find anything
and gets hurt,

24:20.333 --> 24:22.627
and regrets her choice later on?

24:31.511 --> 24:32.679
Ma'am…

24:35.974 --> 24:40.770
All I'm saying is that I don't want
to see her go through hardships.

24:42.147 --> 24:43.940
What's wrong with that?

24:45.066 --> 24:47.986
She may call it

24:48.612 --> 24:52.741
"meddling" and that's fine with me.

24:54.284 --> 24:55.869
If that's what it takes

24:56.828 --> 25:00.874
to keep her from getting hurt.

25:00.957 --> 25:02.709
That's all that matters.

25:10.717 --> 25:12.427
What you're saying…

25:15.847 --> 25:17.807
I don't understand it,

25:19.142 --> 25:20.393
but I get it.

25:22.437 --> 25:24.231
I get that you care about Rin.

25:25.774 --> 25:26.983
So…

25:27.984 --> 25:30.528
please tell Rin what you just said.

25:35.075 --> 25:36.952
What is he saying?

25:39.663 --> 25:42.290
But first…

25:46.044 --> 25:48.171
Have you eaten?

27:43.411 --> 27:44.829
Thank you for waiting.

27:45.955 --> 27:48.291
‎TANOMI

27:49.125 --> 27:52.879
This is the Park family's gimbap
that Rin taught me how to make.

27:54.255 --> 27:56.257
I wanted to serve it to you.

28:02.555 --> 28:03.390
Enjoy.

28:28.164 --> 28:29.999
This is…

28:34.212 --> 28:35.422
Eomma!

28:45.640 --> 28:46.641
Sorry…

28:47.308 --> 28:49.436
Can you please translate

28:49.519 --> 28:51.730
what I'm going to say to your mother?

28:52.480 --> 28:53.690
Huh?

28:54.357 --> 28:56.609
Okay, sure.

29:08.830 --> 29:11.166
I heard from Rin that on the days

29:11.750 --> 29:14.544
you make gimbap,
the whole house smells good,

29:14.627 --> 29:18.089
and it makes her feel very happy.

29:40.153 --> 29:44.240
Rin loves her family more than anything.

29:46.367 --> 29:48.536
When you send her side dishes,

29:48.620 --> 29:52.290
she eats them little by little
and savors each one.

29:52.874 --> 29:55.502
When she sees news
about something happening in Korea,

29:56.044 --> 29:59.714
she immediately writes on her family chat.

30:20.693 --> 30:22.362
To be honest,

30:22.862 --> 30:26.533
I don't have that close of a relationship
with my family.

30:27.408 --> 30:31.287
And so I was a little envious of Rin.

30:33.122 --> 30:34.958
But I think it's beautiful.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.563
In my opinion, Rin is able to do her best

30:57.438 --> 30:59.357
in a foreign land like this

30:59.440 --> 31:02.360
because she has somewhere
she can return to at any time.

31:19.586 --> 31:20.920
So…

31:26.134 --> 31:27.594
Please…

31:30.346 --> 31:34.601
Will you put just a little bit of trust
in the path that Rin chose,

31:35.476 --> 31:37.270
and watch over her?

31:44.944 --> 31:48.031
So, Mom, please…

31:53.328 --> 31:58.207
Will you trust the path that I chose
and watch over me?

32:18.895 --> 32:19.938
Eomma?

32:24.567 --> 32:26.069
Just the thought of you

32:27.362 --> 32:32.200
telling me,
"I don't need your help anymore"

32:33.701 --> 32:37.956
scared me more than anything.

32:41.459 --> 32:42.502
I wished

32:43.294 --> 32:47.882
that you would always look to me for help.

32:48.800 --> 32:51.010
I knew in my head

32:51.594 --> 32:53.721
that it wasn't possible.

32:53.805 --> 32:57.934
But to me,

32:59.394 --> 33:03.398
that is what brings the most happiness.

33:11.864 --> 33:13.199
Eomma…

33:38.266 --> 33:41.436
Make sure you rest well tonight.
Take care.

33:42.520 --> 33:44.731
Thank you for today, Taiga.

33:47.650 --> 33:48.526
How do you say "it was delicious"?

33:54.157 --> 33:55.408
Jeogi…

33:56.701 --> 33:57.869
It was delicious.

34:06.085 --> 34:07.336
Gamsahamnida.

34:19.098 --> 34:20.641
Mom, are you asleep?

34:31.194 --> 34:33.362
I'm sorry I said
horrible things to you today.

34:36.699 --> 34:38.868
I worked as an intern,

34:38.951 --> 34:41.621
and felt like that's where I belonged.

34:42.705 --> 34:45.083
It's my first time feeling that way.

34:48.795 --> 34:51.631
I've made you worry a lot up until now,

34:52.423 --> 34:55.051
so I'll do everything I can to find a job.

34:57.053 --> 34:57.929
Okay?

35:04.060 --> 35:06.729
I don't really understand,

35:09.190 --> 35:11.359
but go ahead and do your best.

35:13.444 --> 35:17.115
If you can't take it anymore,
don't hesitate to tell me.

35:19.659 --> 35:21.702
Thank you, Mom.

35:35.758 --> 35:40.429
TAIGA: DID YOUR MOTHER GET HOME SAFELY?

35:40.513 --> 35:42.682
YEAH. I TOOK HER TO THE AIRPORT.

35:42.765 --> 35:46.936
HOSHIUMI ASAKO - INTERNSHIP

35:48.855 --> 35:49.939
Hello?

35:52.316 --> 35:53.192
Oh, yes.

36:00.491 --> 36:05.037
MY PAGE LOGIN

36:05.121 --> 36:06.289
ACCEPTED

36:09.542 --> 36:10.710
Yes!

36:17.842 --> 36:20.803
Rin! I got accepted!

36:20.887 --> 36:22.889
What? Really?

36:23.764 --> 36:25.558
Congratulations, Taiga.

36:25.641 --> 36:26.809
Thanks.

36:26.893 --> 36:29.854
I'm so glad!

36:32.857 --> 36:34.150
Actually,

36:35.193 --> 36:38.196
I just got a call from work too.

36:39.906 --> 36:40.907
Huh?

36:42.241 --> 36:43.910
I got an offer…

36:46.412 --> 36:48.664
from the Korean advertising company

36:49.415 --> 36:50.875
from the contest the other day.

36:52.335 --> 36:55.504
That's amazing! Congratulations.

36:59.592 --> 37:00.593
Wait…

37:02.220 --> 37:04.931
Did you say "Korean"?

37:09.143 --> 37:10.311
Yeah.

37:17.652 --> 37:19.195
Does that mean…

37:22.740 --> 37:24.242
you're going back?

37:29.914 --> 37:33.125
Maybe.

37:39.840 --> 37:41.050
I see.

37:50.434 --> 37:53.771
I'll be fine.

37:55.398 --> 37:59.318
If this will let you follow
the path you chose, I'm happy.

38:03.322 --> 38:04.573
I told you, remember?

38:05.324 --> 38:07.326
No matter where you go,

38:07.410 --> 38:09.370
I'll make sure I can support you.

38:11.455 --> 38:13.833
But nothing is set yet.

38:14.750 --> 38:16.544
First, I'll do my best at the interview.

38:19.839 --> 38:20.840
You can do it.

38:32.935 --> 38:33.978
PREVIEW

38:34.061 --> 38:35.187
But I…

38:37.064 --> 38:37.898
I…

38:40.359 --> 38:41.736
I was saved by you.

38:41.819 --> 38:42.862
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:42.945 --> 38:43.821
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
